; RocketNet roadmap data. docs/ROADMAP.md is rendered from this file by
; tools/roadmap/render.py (make roadmap); make roadmap-check fails when the
; committed page is not what this renders.
;
; An area declares :columns transports (one column per server transport, in
; the order the automatic ladder ranks them) or :columns platforms (Linux,
; macOS, Windows). A row has one cell per column: y (done and tested there),
; n (not done, or not proven at this release) or - (does not apply). Every y
; cell carries evidence: a CI job that runs there, a test named, or a landed
; commit. :evidence is either one string that names each column it covers,
; or a list of (column "evidence") pairs, one per y cell. Evidence and :note
; stay here; the page shows only the features and the marks.
;
; A document, a model or a proof is checked on Linux and is - on macOS and
; Windows. A row only a Linux job checks (a sanitizer, the nightly soak, the
; examples, a simulation run) is y on Linux and n on macOS and Windows until
; those platforms have a run.
;
; Recorded 2026-10-20 for v1.0.0-preview-1 at 330e951e; source facts rechecked
; at a76d641ad64768e239528cd1c6bfdf37a0caaa41 on 2026-10-22. A landed
; source change is kept distinct from an exact-head platform qualification.
(:title "RocketNet roadmap"
 :text ("Every feature RocketNet has, and every one still to come, by area: a column per transport where a feature is per transport, and a column per platform where it is not. ✅ is done and tested there; ❌ is not done, or not yet proven there; — does not apply. Each table's complete row is the share of ✅ among the cells that apply. Items marked (later) come after the current preview." "Known issues (addressed in the final deliverable) lists what v1.0.0-preview-1 does not yet meet, and how the final deliverable addresses each. Final deliverable: hardening and long testing lists the long runs that come with it.")
 :areas
 ((:id "handshake"
   :title "Connect handshake and security"
   :text "The secure connect of standard/TRANSPORT.md: netcode 1.02 rebuilt on public keys, with every refusal counted."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "Public-key connect tokens: mint, verify and open in the standard's order" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; rocketnet_test_connect_token_frozen, rocketnet_test_connect_token_mint")
    (:feature "Deterministic connect token vectors for minters in other languages" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; e05088e")
    (:feature "6-byte prefilter header with a per-title filter value and epoch" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 52d9be7; rocketnet_test_prefilter")
    (:feature "Cookie gate: bounds, signature, expiry and address checked" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 64ffe20; rocketnet_test_cookie, rocketnet_test_cookie_bounds_signature_verifies")
    (:feature "Cookie key rotates on its period" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 6b60b32, 5e534d4; test_cookie_rotation_draws_a_fresh_key")
    (:feature "Per-connection keys with forward secrecy, secrets wiped on every exit" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; rocketnet_test_connection_keys, rocketnet_test_client_terminal_states_wipe_secrets")
    (:feature "Sealed packets with every refusal proven" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; rocketnet_test_sealed_packets, rocketnet_test_sealed_packet_refusals")
    (:feature "Used-token history and one token, one live connection" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; rocketnet_test_used_token_history, server_admits_sequential_fresh_tokens_past_twice_max_clients, server_refuses_a_token_connected_now")
    (:feature "Admission hook: removed 2026-10-21, it was never in the public API" :cells (- - -) :note "Owner, 2026-10-21: \"delete it. if it's not in the public API right now it probably isn't a real feature.\" It shipped as rocketnet_server_transport_set_admission_callback in the internal layers header only (9eb49a9, rocketnet_test_admission_hook_drops_before_verify); the callback, its type, its constants, its call sites and its tests are deleted. Address validation before asymmetric work is the cookie gate, witnessed by test_request_path_cookie_gate.")
    (:feature "Cheap refusals before crypto: a full server refuses before keypair work" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; PR #248, 4901aba; rocketnet_test_full_server_refuses_before_keypair, rocketnet_test_request_path_cheap_refusals_spend_no_crypto")
    (:feature "Bounded handshake work per update" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 1745d64")
    (:feature "Configurable half-open handshake deadline" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 916239a; rocketnet_test_handshake_deadline_is_configured")
    (:feature "Replay window, cleared whole by a long sequence skip" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; a94f99c, 5ab9e5c; rocketnet_test_replay_protection, rocketnet_test_replay_long_skip_clears_whole_window")
    (:feature "Replay window advances only after the connect check" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 8eab0e0 the slot gate before the replay mark")
    (:feature "Hostile fragment ids cannot poison a reassembly slot" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 4f09049; rocketnet_test_fragment_hostile_id_does_not_poison_slot")
    (:feature "Oversize datagrams are dropped, never truncated" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 611788d, 5321d20; rocketnet_test_receive_drops_oversize_datagram")
    (:feature "Release builds refuse development keys" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; e5d3393; rocketnet_test_dev_keys_refused_in_release")
    (:feature "Release builds do not export development token minting" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 5cc44f4, 1b81ce9; rocketnet_test_dev_token_minting_absent_in_release")
    (:feature "Public API is NULL-safe at the boundary" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 3e51b9d; rocketnet_test_public_api_null_is_a_counted_no_op")
    (:feature "Refusal decisions agree with netcode 1.02" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; e5acbbb")
    (:feature "The token is bound at response open" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; b515ec6; rocketnet_test_token_bound_at_response_open; proofs/tla/RNSecurityTables.tla")
    (:feature "Development keys are off by default and warn on every start" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 6a580ef; dev_keys_warn_on_every_start")
    (:feature "An unauthenticated reply is never larger than its request" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 38caeb2; reply_never_larger_than_request_every_unauthenticated_type, reply_never_larger_than_request_hostile_inputs")
    (:feature "A request with another salt resends the stored challenge" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 43626fc; its cases run in the unit and functional suites ci.yml runs on all three on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164")
    (:feature "Expired-token refusals counted apart, one counter per cause" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 9b0b2ee; its cases run in the unit and functional suites ci.yml runs on all three on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164")
    (:feature "Connect-token create and expire checks can read the game clock" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 9efc7cb; its cases run in the unit and functional suites ci.yml runs on all three on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164")
    (:feature "A backend keypair can be derived from a seed through rocketnet.h" :cells (n n n) :note "not a public rocketnet.h function at this head: tools/exports.txt exports no keypair function and sdk/rocketnet.h names keypair only in a doc comment on the server X25519 keypair (sdk/rocketnet.h:1276). The internal rocketnet_generate_backend_keypair_from_seed in sdk/rocketnet_connect_token.h derives a backend keypair from a seed and is not exported. Commit 5c3b84e8 (the rocketnet.h final API pass) records the public header without this function; the earlier public form landed as b1c5e74 does not state the present public surface")
    (:feature "Attack-surface reduction: a half-finished connection's client slot is checked before its session packet is decrypted" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #427 (df35d02c); test_server_half_open_session_packet_dropped_unopened in tests/test_unit_half_open_session_unopened.cpp, proofs/tla/ReplayWindow.tla (proofs/tla/MCReplayWindowBrokenOpenBeforeGate.cfg); ./bin/test green on all three at 126ef062 and 81b6d3ef (docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-3.md) and in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963" :note "approved 2026-10-21; a spoofer of a client's address loses its 200 lines of reach for half-open targets")
    (:feature "Attack-surface reduction: both sides refuse a connect token with timeout <= 0, and the server's dead allow_negative_timeout is deleted" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #427 (df35d02c); test_client_refuses_token_timeout_zero_or_negative, test_server_refuses_token_timeout_zero_or_negative in tests/test_unit_token_timeout_refused.cpp; ./bin/test green on all three at 126ef062 and 81b6d3ef and in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963" :note "approved 2026-10-21; fail closed, one rule on both sides")
    (:feature "Attack-surface reduction: the XDP filter drops IPv4-options, IPv6 extension-header and later-fragment frames to our port" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed with PR #428 (0a1a2c88); sdk/xdp/server_xdp.c; test_xdp_transport_host_ipv4_options_to_our_port_drop, test_xdp_transport_host_ipv6_extension_headers_to_our_port_drop, test_xdp_transport_host_ipv4_first_fragment_drops_counted, test_xdp_transport_host_ipv6_first_fragment_drops_counted in tests/test_unit_xdp_filter_host.cpp, green in ./bin/test on Linux at 126ef062 and 81b6d3ef and in ci.yml run 40928229963" :note "approved 2026-10-21; no kernel ICMP answers on the game port")
    (:feature "Attack-surface reduction: the pending-wire table is deleted, so an unauthenticated sender holds no state" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #433 (28b409c7); sdk/rocketnet_server_transport.cpp; test_server_connects_after_junk_from_many_sources in tests/test_unit_driver_loopback.cpp; ./bin/test green on all three at 126ef062 and 81b6d3ef and in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963" :note "approved 2026-10-21 (plan #1; owner: security trumps counting request bytes); client stats lose the 3 to 5 handshake packets; one test changes")
    (:feature "Attack-surface reduction: a stateless shape check (prefilter, wire type and size) runs before any per-datagram work" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #433 (28b409c7); sdk/rocketnet_server_transport.cpp; test_server_shape_check_first_on_the_staged_loop, test_server_shape_check_first_on_the_portable_loop in tests/test_unit_driver_loopback.cpp; ./bin/test green on all three at 126ef062 and 81b6d3ef and in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963" :note "approved 2026-10-21 (plan #2); outputs identical")
    (:feature "Attack-surface reduction: the token claim is written only after the signature verifies" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #433 (28b409c7); sdk/rocketnet_server_protocol.cpp; test_claim_written_only_after_signature_verifies in tests/test_unit_handshake_witness.cpp; proofs/tla/ReceiveOrder.tla (ClaimOnlyAfterSignature, proofs/tla/MCReceiveOrderBrokenClaimBeforeSignature.cfg); ./bin/test green on all three at 126ef062 and 81b6d3ef and in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963" :note "approved 2026-10-21 (plan #3); outputs identical; proofs/tla/ReceiveOrder.tla splits the claim (ClaimOnlyAfterSignature)")
    (:feature "Attack-surface reduction: a token created beyond the 30-second clock-skew allowance is refused, and the lifetime cap that has no setting is deleted" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #433 (28b409c7) and raised to 30 seconds in sdk/rocketnet_server_protocol.cpp; test_token_created_past_skew_is_refused, test_token_created_within_skew_passes_the_rung, test_token_create_skew_enforced_without_lifetime_cap in tests/test_unit_handshake_witness.cpp and test_token_created_at_the_skew_limit_is_accepted, test_token_with_a_long_lifetime_is_accepted, test_token_future_creation_without_lifetime_limit in tests/test_unit_token_time_refusals.cpp; ./bin/test green on all three at 126ef062 and 81b6d3ef and in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963" :note "approved 2026-10-21 (plan #4); landed with PR #433 (28b409c7) with a five-second allowance. Preview-3 raises the explicit future-skew allowance in sdk/rocketnet_server_protocol.cpp to 30 seconds; this closes the beyond-allowance part of the known issue on replayed responses and token claims")
    (:feature "ROCKETNET_DEVELOPMENT is renamed ROCKETNET_DEV, default 1; a production build sets ROCKETNET_DEV=0" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #431 (ea78ee8f) and #610 (c8386ae0); sdk/rocketnet.h defines ROCKETNET_DEV (default 1); both ROCKETNET_DEV=ON and ROCKETNET_DEV=OFF builds and suites pass on all three at 126ef062 and 81b6d3ef (docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-3.md) and in ci.yml runs 40923772759 and 40925425656" :note "Owner, 2026-10-21: keyed off the define, not debug or release. The two rows below key off it; landed with PR #431")
    (:feature "With ROCKETNET_DEV=0, test and development code is compiled out: the network simulator, the test seams, the development config and the development server secret key" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #431 (ea78ee8f) and #610 (c8386ae0); tools/check_exports.py, tools/check_test_scaffolding_boundary.py and tools/check_dll_consumer.py in ci.yml on all three, green in runs 40923772759 and 40925425656" :note "approved 2026-10-21 (plan #5); landed with PR #431; outputs identical; the key bytes in the shipped library go from 1 to 0")
    (:feature "With ROCKETNET_DEV=0, both sides refuse the published test packet filter, and the client refuses tokens sealed with the development keys" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #431 (ea78ee8f); test_production_server_refuses_test_packet_filter, test_production_client_refuses_test_packet_filter, test_production_client_refuses_dev_connect_token in tests/test_unit_production_refusals.cpp, run in ROCKETNET_DEV=OFF builds on all three in ci.yml runs 40923772759, 40925425656 and 40932598827" :note "approved 2026-10-21 (plan #6); landed with PR #431: the rule moved onto ROCKETNET_DEV and the client refuses too")
    (:feature "AGENTS.md has a Before production section: what a production build sets and refuses" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: a document; landed with PR #431 (ea78ee8f); docs/AGENTS.md Before production section, checked by tools/docs/check_agents_md.sh in docs.yml (green in run 40932599020 at c5f85ea4)" :note "a document; approved 2026-10-21 with the ROCKETNET_DEV rows; landed with PR #431")
    (:feature "The client trusts only the server: the idle timer and the RTT sample come only from the authenticated challenge, never the clear-salt cookie, and the client socket is connected" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #434 (ec85cce2) and 57ef874d; test_client_cookie_does_not_refresh_idle_timer, test_client_transport_connects_socket_to_server, test_client_transport_refuses_when_connect_fails, test_client_cookie_takes_no_rtt_sample, test_client_forged_cookie_never_displaces_kept_cookie in tests/test_unit_client_trusts_only_server.cpp; proofs/tla/ClientConnection.tla (proofs/tla/MCClientConnectionCookieTrust.cfg); ./bin/test green on all three at 126ef062 and 81b6d3ef and in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963" :note "approved 2026-10-21 (plan #9); landed with PR #434 (ec85cce2); off-server datagrams are dropped by the kernel")
    (:feature "Portable server and client transports are available in production; native server transports remain preferred" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 7be9f52e; sdk/rocketnet_drivers.inc ranks portable at (ROCKETNET_DEV ? 30 : 50) on the server and 30 on the client; functional_production (auto ladder and portable pinned) and tests/test_driver.cpp pass on all three in ci.yml runs 40923772759, 40925425656 and 40932598827" :note "The owner enabled portable servers in production on 2026-10-22 for backend key generation and production end-to-end functional verification; this supersedes the earlier production server exclusion. Native server transports remain first in production auto selection")
    (:feature "Session layer: identity auth with a backend, rolling magic, keyed filter value (later)" :cells (n n n) :note "in part: the design is docs/SESSION.md (eb22aab), the keyed filter value and its two-generation epoch window are in (8e99124 keyed_filter_value_known_answers; ce1b1a0 filter_epoch_window_accepts_two_generations; proofs/tla/RNFilterEpochs.tla 4ea64ce), and one token holds one live connection (eef77ac); the backend identity auth and the rolling magic are not built. v2, optional, after v1.0.0-preview-1. The 6-byte header with its epoch byte is already in, so the keyed form is a configuration change, not a wire break. It needs a backend that tracks the connected set across servers live: one identity, one seat, so a shared token gives away the sharer's own slot, and the old player is kicked with rocketnet_server_transport_disconnect_client when the same user hash appears elsewhere. An extraction from a production backend, not a new design. Then the rolling magic feeds the keyed filter value (SipHash over type, length and the four bytes after the header, one MAC per packet), and a per-title generator emits the constant and the keyed reader in every language plus verifier-clean BPF behind a differential gate. Never: a default magic, or standalone IP pinning")))
  (:id "connection"
   :title "Connections and the connection layer"
   :text "The unreliable connection layer the message layer runs over: connection state, slots, keep-alives, fragments, acks and the server loop."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "Client connection state machine with every timeout pairing" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; rocketnet_test_client_timeout_paths; proofs/tla/ClientConnection.tla 3afa363")
    (:feature "Server client slots from a free-slot stack" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; c40f599; rocketnet_test_client_slots; proofs/tla/ServerConnection.tla eb57f2d")
    (:feature "Encryption mappings with handshake and idle deadlines" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; rocketnet_test_encryption_map, rocketnet_test_server_update_sweep")
    (:feature "Keep-alives paced and suppressed by traffic" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; rocketnet_test_client_keep_alive_suppression")
    (:feature "Payloads both ways from the connection response on" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; rocketnet_test_client_payload_before_first_keep_alive")
    (:feature "Redundant disconnect burst, from the client or the server" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; rocketnet_test_client_disconnect_reports_state_change; rocketnet_server_transport_disconnect_client")
    (:feature "Large payloads fragmented and reassembled" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 7e959ab; rocketnet_test_fragment_vector; reassembly geometry under a 512 MiB component budget, oversized configurations refused before any allocation: test_lifecycle.cpp check_memory_geometry")
    (:feature "Fragments accepted only on a connected slot" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 9e0d822")
    (:feature "Server transport entries carry a connection id" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 65bab41; rocketnet_test_server_transport_entries_carry_connection_id")
    (:feature "Per-packet acks with delivery notification" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 8af8b80; rocketnet_test_ack_block_validity, rocketnet_test_ack_block_build")
    (:feature "Ack history that survives a long lossy path" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 187a875; rocketnet_test_send_history_lossy_long_path; ROCKETNET_HISTORY_PACKETS 4096 default, 4096 to 32768 (sdk/rocketnet_history.h), no frame, send or ack rate assumed; test_lifecycle.cpp check_ack_retention, rocketnet_test_send_history_silent_receiver_overflows")
    (:feature "Frame sync: a fixed-rate server loop with priority and drop detection" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; rocketnet_test_frame_sync_advance, rocketnet_test_frame_sync_guard")
    (:feature "Counters on every path, each classified, conserved and named by a test" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 1750e83; cumulative per-connection wire totals af8c0b0 and race-free 800119c (wire_totals_count_every_packet_and_byte, rocketnet_test_transport_wire_totals_concurrent_send_exact); rocketnet_num_counters and rocketnet_counter_value for FFI callers; packet-rate statistics in elapsed-time buckets: test_lifecycle.cpp check_stats_cadence")
    (:feature "The server drains its receive queue up to a per-update budget" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as c61badc; its cases run in the unit and functional suites ci.yml runs on all three on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164")
    (:feature "Every piece of per-connection state is reset when a connection ends, in one function per side" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 9043173; its cases run in the unit and functional suites ci.yml runs on all three on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164")
    (:feature "A public client can run with no I/O thread, stepped by the caller's update" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 16a7c0a; its cases run in the unit and functional suites ci.yml runs on all three on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164")
    (:feature "Client socket I/O off the main thread, gated by the measured main-thread cost per frame" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux: a60ed16 rocketnet_test_client_io_linux_handoff_round_trip and the Linux CI; macOS: 151508f rocketnet_test_client_io_apple_handoff_round_trip, run on macOS; Windows: 8ddc93e rocketnet_test_client_io_windows_handoff_round_trip, run on Windows; docs/CLIENT-IO.md b0b4527, proofs/tla/RNClientIo.tla; 4f8a8e9 client_io_backend_with_wait_uses_io_thread; Linux a60ed16, Apple 151508f, Windows 8ddc93e (rocketnet_test_client_io_linux_handoff_round_trip, rocketnet_test_client_io_apple_handoff_round_trip, rocketnet_test_client_io_windows_handoff_round_trip); decrypt off the main thread c236806; the 100 us gate 20d8b35, benchmarks/client_main_thread_cost.md, .github/workflows/nightly-frame-budget.yml f12db2b")))
