  (:id "messages"
   :title "Channels, sending and memory"
   :text "The message layer of standard/MESSAGES.md: channels, priorities, budgets and one fixed region per connection."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "Zero-copy send: start, write in place, finish or abort" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 2c1aa7b; reliable_sequenced_c_api_start_finish")
    (:feature "An unreliable message that fits one packet is written in place in that packet, with no copy" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 81ecfcff, 3721c1fd, 455f3639, 771dce32 and 1719e973; test_unreliable_fit_is_written_in_the_packet, test_unreliable_fit_in_place_every_transport, test_unreliable_fit_has_no_message_copy, test_unreliable_over_fit_takes_the_message_buffer, test_in_place_unreliable_keeps_acks_and_order in tests/test_unit_unreliable_in_place.cpp; ./bin/test green on all three at 126ef062 and 81b6d3ef and in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Receive and release messages as views" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 2c1aa7b; unreliable_delivered_as_a_view; proofs/tla/RNSlots.tla")
    (:feature "N channels with per-record dispatch" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; c79da45")
    (:feature "Large reliable messages split into blocks and delivered whole" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 16531dd; reliable_sequenced_block_delivers_whole, ordered_receipt_after_all_chunks")
    (:feature "Four send priorities, round robin across channels" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 273cc81, e0733e5; higher_priority_first_within_class")
    (:feature "Small messages aggregated into packets" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; c79da45; builder_obeys_budget_and_class_order")
    (:feature "Send budget in kbps per connection" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; a4ff908; budgets_are_per_connection; a configured default 8d9b806 (send_budget_defaults_from_config, send_budget_env_overrides_config)")
    (:feature "Resend delay from the measured round trip, block chunks paced by it, no backoff" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; f6a3068, 2322d7c; resend_delay_is_min_of_interval_and_rtt, no_backoff_between_resends, chunk_resend_paced_by_rtt_not_interval; proofs/tla/RNResendTiming.tla")
    (:feature "A 1400-byte game message fits one packet" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; ff4c7c6; message_of_1400_bytes_is_one_unfragmented_packet")
    (:feature "Message layer: one fixed region per connection, no allocation after create" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 8b99c72; no_allocation_after_create")
    (:feature "Caller-supplied memory block" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; user_block_is_used_and_nothing_else; aligned allocation keeps its callback and context, late replacement refused: rocketnet_test_allocator_refusal_is_returned, test_lifecycle.cpp check_component_create_sweeps")
    (:feature "Memory exhaustion kicks only that connection" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; c335529; server_kicks_exhausted_client_others_unaffected")
    (:feature "Hostile records and chunks refused" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; d1ff1a2; hostile_chunk_count_or_index_kicks, hostile_small_at_held_ordering_is_refused")
    (:feature "Endpoint and slots as pure machines" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; bbb62e8 endpoint_back_to_back_over_lossy_array, endpoint_never_allocates_or_reads_a_clock; 9bca948 slots_observe_and_admit; proofs/tla/RNEndpoint.tla 3c3c048")
    (:feature "CONFIG announcement: both ends prove the same configuration" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 1026843 message_config_equal_connects_and_verifies, message_config_mismatch_ends_both_connections; functional 4906e5d")
    (:feature "Message layer soaked at full configured load" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: bounded exhaustion soak c335529, the many-client load harness bin/load (docs/LOAD.md, f49cc28), .github/workflows/nightly-soak.yml on Linux, macOS and Windows, and the recorded 1800 s per-transport soaks in docs/runs/linux-soak-30min-per-transport.md (adca4345), docs/runs/macos-soak-per-transport.md (31ad7862), docs/runs/windows-soak-native-server.md (3f900fa1) and docs/runs/windows-soak-portable.md (74b8bb7f), qualified in docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-3.md")
    (:feature "Broadcast send" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 7e2106e; message_server_broadcast_reaches_every_connected, message_server_broadcast_skips_free_and_exhausted")
    (:feature "The unreleased-message refusal is a public counter on client and server" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 5a6cc45; its cases run in the unit and functional suites ci.yml runs on all three on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164")
    (:feature "The channel documentation names the counter an oversize unreliable send moves" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: a document; landed as 1ad9b49")
    (:feature "Flows: server-side subscription groups (later)" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/REQUIREMENTS.md step 3; designed and modelled, not built: docs/FLOWS.md, proofs/tla/RNFlows.tla (2c7236b)")))
  (:id "transports"
   :title "Transports"
   :text ("The server transports below the connection layer, one column each, in the order the automatic ladder ranks them: xdp, gso, io_uring and portable on Linux, msgx and portable on macOS, portable, iocp and rio on Windows. Portable server and client I/O are available in both builds. Production Windows servers rank iocp and rio ahead of portable. The per-endpoint ROCKETNET_SERVER_TRANSPORT and ROCKETNET_CLIENT_TRANSPORT select one at runtime; loopback is pin-only." "AF_XDP serves IPv4 and IPv6 end to end (8a35a14, 5558a70b): a server serves the family of its public address, and the ladder offers xdp for either." "— is a transport the feature does not apply to: xdp bypasses the kernel's UDP stack, loopback is in-process, and a row that names one transport's own mechanism is — for the others." "Portable remains a fallback rather than a performance target. The owner enabled it in production on 2026-10-22; the earlier performance guidance remains (2026-10-21: \"now on both client and server we can ignore the portable transport because it is not a production transport. Don't make it slow for no reason, but don't over optimize or worry too much about it.\"). The production performance targets are for the native transports; the portable column still records what portable does.")
   :columns transports
   :rows
   ((:feature "Server transport" :cells (y y y y y y y y) :evidence ((xdp "c0b0928; the xdp rows of the XDP table") (msgx "8d54e30") (gso "0801c9a; test_gso_transport_server_wire_ipv6, test_gso_transport_server_wire_dual_stack") (io_uring "f7cfe0f and 7be058d (test_io_uring_transport_server_probe, test_io_uring_transport_server_wire_ipv4, test_io_uring_transport_server_wire_ipv6, test_io_uring_transport_server_wire_dual_stack, test_io_uring_transport_server_send_overflow, test_io_uring_transport_server_receive_rearms_after_no_buffers)") (portable "ci.yml runs ./bin/functional with the portable rung pinned on the ubuntu-24.04 Debug and Release (b) legs, green in runs 39271096164 and 39286548764; rocketnet_server_socket_linux.cpp") (iocp "45da97d and 038131eb; build-and-test-windows in ci.yml runs the unit, functional and transport family matrix suites with iocp, green in runs 40923772759, 40925425656 and 40932598827; docs/runs/windows-transport-family-50x-native.md (689f0947)") (rio "367a33f, 1dcb6b8 (rocketnet_test_server_rio_probe, rocketnet_test_server_rio_wire_ipv4, rocketnet_test_server_rio_wire_ipv6, rocketnet_test_server_rio_wire_dual_stack, rocketnet_test_server_rio_send_full; proofs/tla/RNRioDriver.tla 5255a0d)") (loopback "bfcb888 (driver_loopback_binds_and_discovers_a_port, driver_loopback_exchanges_both_ways, driver_loopback_full_queue_drops_and_counts, driver_loopback_destroy_frees_the_port)")))
    (:feature "Selectable by pin at runtime" :cells (y y y y y y y y) :evidence ((xdp "10308e4 test_xdp_transport_server_io_pin") (msgx "10308e4 test_msgx_transport_server_io_pin") (gso "10308e4 test_gso_transport_server_io_pin") (io_uring "2d2c057 test_io_uring_transport_server_io_pin") (portable "10308e4 test_portable_transport_server_io_pin") (iocp "10308e4 test_iocp_transport_server_io_pin") (rio "0c31bf7 test_rio_transport_server_io_pin") (loopback "5d059d8 and 1c6f91a (test_transport_pin_only, test_loopback_transport_server_io_pin, test_loopback_transport_env_pins)")))
    (:feature "IPv6 and dual-stack binds" :cells (y y y y y y y y) :evidence ((xdp "8a35a14 and 5558a70b; xdp_frame_parse_ipv6_udp and xdp_ladder_keeps_xdp_for_ipv6 in ./bin/test, and test_xdp_transport_max_size_both_ways_ipv4 and test_xdp_transport_max_size_both_ways_ipv6 pass end to end in docs/runs/xdp-ipv6-end-to-end.md (3a04ed7a) and in ci.yml's transport family matrix") (msgx "202ef32 and 31f4050; test_loopback_transport_ipv6 and test_transport_dual_stack_ipv4_client in ci.yml's transport family matrix on macOS (green in runs 40925425656 and 40928229963) and docs/runs/macos-transport-cells-50x.md (13b7b291)") (gso "test_gso_transport_server_wire_ipv6, test_gso_transport_server_wire_dual_stack in the Linux CI") (io_uring "7be058d test_io_uring_transport_server_wire_ipv6, test_io_uring_transport_server_wire_dual_stack in the Linux CI") (portable "ci.yml runs ./bin/functional with ROCKETNET_SERVER_TRANSPORT=portable on Linux, holding test_loopback_transport_ipv6") (iocp "202ef32 and 31f4050; test_loopback_transport_ipv6 and test_transport_dual_stack_ipv4_client in ci.yml's transport family matrix on Windows (green in runs 40923772759 and 40925425656) and docs/runs/windows-transport-family-50x-native.md (689f0947)") (rio "1dcb6b8 rocketnet_test_server_rio_wire_ipv6, rocketnet_test_server_rio_wire_dual_stack, run on Windows") (loopback "202ef32 and 31f4050; test_loopback_transport_ipv6 and test_transport_dual_stack_ipv4_client in ci.yml's transport family matrix on Linux, macOS and Windows (green in runs 40923772759 and 40925425656), docs/runs/linux-transport-cells-50x.md (ac4206a6), docs/runs/macos-transport-cells-50x.md (13b7b291) and docs/runs/windows-transport-family-50x.md (b225201d)")))
    (:feature "Receive coalescing by the kernel (UDP_GRO on Linux, URO on Windows), split by stride" :cells (- n y y n y n -) :evidence ((gso "the gso driver enables UDP_GRO per socket and splits by the stride cmsg; GRO_BATCHES in the gso wire case") (io_uring "d0984512 and 5db7238c; sdk/rocketnet_server_uring_linux.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_uring_codec.h, tests/test_unit_uring_codec.cpp, proofs/tla/RNUringDriver.tla") (iocp "a8ffbac rocketnet_test_server_iocp_uso_uro_probe; the coalesce codec 7df4c3c coalesce_split_by_stride_round_trips")) :note "msgx, portable and rio receive one datagram per call today")
    (:feature "Send segmentation by the kernel (UDP GSO on Linux, USO on Windows), probed with fallback" :cells (- n y y n y n -) :evidence ((gso "0801c9a the gso transport; the gso wire case") (io_uring "d0984512 and 5db7238c; sdk/rocketnet_server_uring_linux.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_uring_codec.h, tests/test_unit_uring_codec.cpp, proofs/tla/RNUringDriver.tla") (iocp "a8ffbac; rocketnet_test_server_iocp_uso_uro_probe, rocketnet_test_server_iocp_uso_wire; the coalesce codec 7df4c3c (coalesce_split_by_stride_round_trips)")) :note "msgx, portable and rio send one datagram per call today")
    (:feature "Registered I/O (RIO) on Windows" :cells (- - - - - - y -) :evidence ((rio "367a33f, 1dcb6b8, 0c31bf7; rocketnet_test_server_rio_wire_ipv4, rocketnet_test_server_driver_pin_rio; proofs/tla/RNRioDriver.tla 5255a0d; the rio column of Server transport")))
    (:feature "The loopback transport holds max clients plus the server" :cells (- - - - - - - y) :evidence ((loopback "ad98d7b landed, tested on Linux")))
    (:feature "The loopback transport allocates its queues up front, never while traffic flows" :cells (- - - - - - - y) :evidence ((loopback "landed as 49cc8384; transport_loopback_runtime_does_not_allocate green in ./bin/test at 330e951e in a Release build on Linux x86_64")))))
  (:id "xdp"
   :title "XDP (later)"
   :text ("The AF_XDP server transport, the xdp column; every other column is —. Further XDP work comes after v1.0.0-preview-1; RocketNet has run live with AF_XDP in copy mode: 60-second non-timing correctness rungs at 1, 10, 100, 500 and 1000 clients (415e796d, runtime source a76d641a; docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-2.md) and a 1000-client LAN proof for 300 s on a 10000 Mb/s server NIC with minimum per-client uplink 283.96 kbps, delivery pass, timing verdict FAIL (docs/runs/lan-1000-proof-xdp.md, head 534cce2e). No record in this repository measures 10 Gbps throughput; zero-copy and line-rate performance are unqualified (docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-2.md, docs/LIVE-XDP.md).")
   :columns transports
   :rows
   ((:feature "Kernel prefilter with AF_XDP rings and counted verdicts" :cells (y - - - - - - -) :evidence ((xdp "c0b0928; xdp_host_every_counter_has_a_case; libxdp all-or-zero reservation, send pressure retains the staged packet, no worker exits: test_lifecycle.cpp check_frame_conservation, check_send_handoff")))
    (:feature "Native attach on a production NIC with internet handshakes" :cells (y - - - - - - -) :evidence ((xdp "8d54514")))
    (:feature "Kernel filter decisions run as host C in the unit suite" :cells (y - - - - - - -) :evidence ((xdp "bf2aecd")))
    (:feature "Kernel filter counters through the transport counter surface" :cells (y - - - - - - -) :evidence ((xdp "394dc9f the prefilter counter capability; 5d736db the xdp driver adapter; prefilter_counters_map_each_kernel_counter, prefilter_counters_are_assigned_not_added, prefilter_counters_xdp_driver_reports_them")) :note "the live per-CPU read through a committed XDP socket is exercised only on the dedicated XDP machine")
    (:feature "Kernel replay protection with a read-only high-water map" :cells (y - - - - - - -) :evidence ((xdp "bace052 proofs/tla/RNXdpReplay.tla; 7013a56 kernel rule and xdp_host_replay_never_writes_the_map, xdp_host_replay_drops_behind_the_window; 26f2fac socket writer; 22f87a9 transport walk; 4f1d2a9 xdp_host_replay_table_set_get_reset; 3e1fd05 replay_drops_behind_the_window, replay_never_writes_the_map, replay_key_layout_matches_header; 306bd2b standard/TRANSPORT.md or standard/MESSAGES.md sizing")))
    (:feature "The standard sizes the kernel replay map apart from the userspace replay window" :cells (y - - - - - - -) :evidence ((xdp "c1a6ff2; standard/TRANSPORT.md or standard/MESSAGES.md Replay window sizing (ROCKETNET_XDP_REPLAY_WINDOW)")))
    (:feature "AF_XDP bind requests zero-copy" :cells (y - - - - - - -) :evidence ((xdp "6bb1361; xdp_socket_config_requests_zero_copy_at_bind")) :note "this proves the bind request, not the negotiated live mode. 415e796d, with SDK and load-harness inputs identical at runtime source a76d641a, ran live in copy mode for 60-second correctness rungs at 1, 10, 100, 500 and 1000 clients; docs/runs/xdp-zero-copy.md at 010c8167de062d24dafcdf9153577b2b8e078760 records verdict HOLD: the bench NIC refuses the zero-copy bind, so zero-copy remains unqualified")
    (:feature "Replies go to the client's own MAC address on link, to the gateway otherwise" :cells (y - - - - - - -) :evidence ((xdp "f435279 landed, tested on Linux")))
    (:feature "AF_XDP on AWS GameLift fleets: the research" :cells (y - - - - - - -) :evidence ((xdp "6930277 docs/GAMELIFT.md")))
    (:feature "The live stress runner: the client stress mode and the merge" :cells (y - - - - - - -) :evidence ((xdp "211833e landed, tested on Linux")))
    (:feature "The live stress runner: the server stress mode" :cells (y - - - - - - -) :evidence ((xdp "1d4af4c landed, tested on Linux")))
    (:feature "Preview-2 live AF_XDP copy-mode correctness at 1, 10, 100, 500 and 1000 clients" :cells (y - - - - - - -) :evidence ((xdp "415e796d, with SDK and load-harness inputs identical at runtime source a76d641a: non-timing correctness passed for 60 seconds at every rung and XDP detached after each run")) :note "timing is separate: upper-bound p99 was 39, 58, 497, 1003 and 2282 microseconds at 1, 10, 100, 500 and 1000 clients")
    (:feature "Packet blaster and simulated-client harnesses at line rate" :cells (y - - - - - - -) :evidence ((xdp "8c75c956 and 5192ff68; docs/XDP-PACKET-BLASTER.md, tools/xdp_packet_blaster.c, tools/xdp_packet_blaster.h, tools/xdp_packet_blaster_cases.json and tools/test_xdp_packet_blaster.py; live runner scripts 51f0fae, docs/LIVE-XDP.md and proofs/tla/RNLiveFleetRun.tla bb9b36e")) :note "the packet blaster and simulated-client harnesses are landed and tested; the live 10 Gbps line-rate run is tracked in the throughput row below")
    (:feature "Ownership and retry paths regression-validated against a recorded throughput baseline" :cells (n - - - - - - -) :note "no throughput baseline is recorded in this repository: the recorded AF_XDP evidence is copy-mode correctness (60-second rungs at 1-1000 clients, 415e796d; 1000-client LAN proof, docs/runs/lan-1000-proof-xdp.md), and line-rate performance is unqualified, so this validation is owed against a provisioned deployment; CI runs no privileged XDP traffic and test executables forbid privileged commit")
    (:feature "Privileged syscall-failure coverage in its own lab" :cells (n - - - - - - -) :note "targeted syscall-failure and frame-conservation tests cover different conditions from throughput tests")
    (:feature "The live stress run: the XDP server against one client from every test machine (later)" :cells (n - - - - - - -) :note "planned after v1.0.0-preview-1")))
  (:id "transport-load"
   :title "Throughput and load per transport"
   :text ("One server per transport on a LAN, measured: a row per server platform, a cell per transport that platform runs; — is a transport the platform does not run, and loopback is in-process.")
   :columns transports
   :rows
   ((:feature "LAN throughput, a Linux server" :cells (n - n n - - - -) :note "docs/runs/lan-1000-proof.md records Linux gso and io_uring at 1ca477339e150220f90e96bbe7c61be5b175eb51 for 600 seconds and xdp copy mode at 534cce2e10159b52074ea9b10f7a2f0b074f7298 for 300 seconds, each with 1000 clients over the LAN and every reliability mode and size class passing the delivery checks; timing_verdict is FAIL in each record, so these connection-and-delivery records do not qualify throughput and no cell turns green on them. The portable LAN cell is void: the proof covers native server transports only (ruling of 2026-10-24)")
