    (:feature "CBMC proves the client packet readers free of out-of-bounds access up to the full packet size (later)" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed as d771e03c and 18ff2e87; proofs/cbmc/proof_connect_token_read.c, proofs/cbmc/proof_packet_prefilter_open.c, proofs/cbmc/proof_fragment_reassembly.c, proofs/cbmc/proof_message_read_max.c, proofs/cbmc/INVENTORY.md, proofs/cbmc/full-bounds-results.md and .github/workflows/cbmc.yml, green in run 40937422460")
    (:feature "CBMC proves the sequence buffers and replay window free of out-of-bounds access (later)" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed as 4d58844, d771e03c and 18ff2e87; proofs/cbmc/proof_replay_advance.c, proofs/cbmc/proof_window_send.c, proofs/cbmc/proof_window_receive.c, proofs/cbmc/proof_window_ack.c, proofs/cbmc/INVENTORY.md, proofs/cbmc/full-bounds-partition-results.md, proofs/cbmc/full-bounds-recovery-results.md and .github/workflows/cbmc.yml, green in run 40937422460")
    (:feature "ESBMC proofs: every rocketnet_assert on the proved paths is a checked property (later)" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed as d771e03c and 18ff2e87; proofs/cbmc/harness.h maps rocketnet_assert to __CPROVER_assert on all proved harnesses, checked by .github/workflows/cbmc.yml and .github/workflows/nightly-proofs.yml, green in run 40937422460")
    (:feature "The proof tools and Frama-Clang prerequisites in place before the Frama-Clang trial (later)" :cells (n - -) :note "planned after v1.0.0-preview-1")
    (:feature "Frama-Clang trial: can WP prove rocketnet_ack_block_read from the C++ source? (later)" :cells (n - -) :note "planned after v1.0.0-preview-1")
    (:feature "The MSan known-findings list matches every toolchain the runners use (later)" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed as 242cd591, afadbfab, f825ef97 and 81b6d3ef (#600); tools/run_msan.sh, tools/test_run_msan.py and tests/msan_scale_allocator.h, verified on clang 18 and clang 21 in msan.yml (green in run 40937422503)")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 6: the keyed filter value is compared under AddressSanitizer against a direct eight-byte SipHash reference" :cells (- - -) :note "retired in #607 (1bcca824): rocketnet_keyed_filter_value had no SDK caller and was deleted with tests/test_unit_keyed_filter_value.cpp")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 7: received-bandwidth high time after receive-tail eviction matches the reference recompute" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 7 (quality): omitting the stats_received_high_time update after unlinking the receive-time tail survives at sdk/rocketnet_ack.cpp; receive three records with distinct times, advance out the newest-time tail, and compare with the reference recompute")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 8: overwriting a zero RTT sample keeps the RTT count and minimum exact" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 8 (quality): treating an old zero RTT sample as counted survives at sdk/rocketnet_ack.cpp; write a zero sample into one history slot, overwrite it with a positive sample, and expect count 1 and the positive minimum")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 9: acknowledging the packet exactly at the loss-eligible top keeps packet loss exact" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 9 (quality): the loss-eligible upper bound surviving as < instead of <= at sdk/rocketnet_ack.cpp leaves stats_eligible_unacked one high; send half a retained window plus one packet, ACK only the eligible-top sequence, and compare with the reference recompute")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 10: an empty ACK block reconciles the newest sequence's bitmap bits" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 10 (quality): reconciliation skipping highest_sequence survives at sdk/rocketnet_ack.cpp; corrupt only the newest sequence's bitmap bits, process an empty ACK block, and expect both bitmaps restored to the ring state")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 11: the reference recompute's received-bandwidth span matches a direct min/max-time calculation" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 11 (quality): omitting finish = record->receive_time for the first received record survives at sdk/rocketnet_ack.cpp; recompute a history whose first visited record has the latest receive time")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 12: the ack allocation-size helper returns zero for zero clients" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 12 (quality): the allocation-size helper accepting zero clients survives at sdk/rocketnet_ack.cpp; expect allocation bytes 0 for clients 0 and nonzero for clients 1")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 13: the server delivered-capacity helper returns zero for zero slots" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 13 (quality): the delivered-capacity helper accepting zero slots survives at sdk/rocketnet_fragment.cpp; expect capacity 0 for (max_clients, 0) and positive for (max_clients, 1)")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 14: maximum-sized non-final fragments are size-checked before the final fragment arrives" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 14 (quality): replacing the unseen-final sentinel -1 with zero survives at sdk/rocketnet_fragment.cpp; start a maximum-sized payload with non-final fragments while the final is absent, then test the one-byte boundary before and after the final arrives")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 15: the send-arena allocation helper returns zero for a zero dimension" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 15 (quality): rocketnet_send_arena_allocation_bytes accepting zero bytes per slot survives at sdk/rocketnet_fragment.cpp; expect (1, 0) and (0, 1) to return 0 and (1, 1) nonzero")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 16: the arena ownership check refuses the one-past-end pointer" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 16 (quality): the arena ownership upper bound surviving as <= end instead of < end at sdk/rocketnet_fragment.cpp claims the one-past-end pointer as owned; expect ownership for data and data + size - 1 and none for data + size")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 17: opening a packet with a mismatched ephemeral key returns a negative error both ways" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 17 (quality): the ephemeral-key mismatch path returning zero instead of a negative error survives at sdk/rocketnet_protocol.cpp; open a type that excludes an ephemeral key with a non-null key and a type that requires one with null, and require a negative result both times")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 18: an ACK finds a packet sitting in its home hash slot" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 18 (quality): starting the open-addressed lookup at probe 1 survives at sdk/rocketnet_window_ack.cpp; insert one packet into an otherwise empty sent index and ACK it, expecting it found and released")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 19: reference-head advancement in normal reclaim and forced eviction keeps ref_tail - ref_head exact" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 19 (quality): omitting reference-head advancement during normal reclaim and subtracting it during forced eviction survive at sdk/rocketnet_window_ack.cpp; cover an acknowledged head reclaim and a full-map eviction, checking ref_tail - ref_head equals the references held by live packets after each step")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 20: a reset ACK map starts with an empty packet and reference map" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 20 (quality): initializing pkt_tail to 1 survives at sdk/rocketnet_window_ack.cpp; after reset require an empty map, then send and ACK one packet, checking head and tail move from zero to one together")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 21: development resend-gap diagnostics report each class's count and gap bounds exactly" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 21 (quality): six diagnostic mutants survive at sdk/rocketnet_window_ack.cpp; in a development build, resend one message and one chunk across three updates including a repeated timestamp and assert each class's count, minimum gap, early minimum and late maximum")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 22: the batch-ACK entry refuses a null packet-id array with a positive count" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 22 (quality): the batch-ACK guard surviving as && instead of || at sdk/rocketnet_window_ack.cpp would dereference a null packet-id array; call with (NULL, 1) and expect zero matches without a crash, retaining the empty non-null case")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 23: a reused receive descriptor starts with no fragment-block state" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 23 (quality): a reused receive descriptor starting with block_have = 1 or a retained block_count survives at sdk/rocketnet_window_receive.cpp; wrap the receive window once with a fragmented message, then accept a plain message into the same descriptor and require both fields zero")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 24: duplicate and out-of-window ACKs report no newly matched ACK" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 24 (quality): an invalid or duplicate ACK returning success from rn_window_send_mark_acked survives at sdk/rocketnet_window_send.cpp; ACK one live number twice and one number outside the window and require results 1, 0 and 0")
    (:feature "Mutation audit finding 25: releasing the oldest number clears a stalled reliable send window, releasing another does not" :cells (n n n) :note "docs/audits/2026-10-24-mutation-testing.md finding 25 (quality): negating the test that clears stalled when U_prime advances survives at sdk/rocketnet_window_send.cpp; fill the window to stall and release the oldest number expecting stalled == 0, and release a non-oldest number expecting it to remain set")))
  (:id "platforms"
   :title "Platforms"
   :text "Where RocketNet builds and passes. Every push runs the unit and functional suites on Linux and macOS; on Windows every push runs the unit suite, the lifecycle binary, the native driver contract and the transport family matrix, and the whole functional suite runs in the nightly tier (about 223 s, over the per-commit bound). The nightly jobs run on Linux, macOS and Windows."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "Per-commit CI, Debug and Release" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs on Linux (Debug and Release), macOS (Debug and Release) and Windows (Release per push in ci.yml, Debug in nightly.yml build-and-test-windows-debug at 20e2a9a4 and 20f5c63d), green across all three in ci.yml runs 40923772759, 40925425656, 40928229963 and 40932598827 (038131eb, 980fb9c6)")
    (:feature "Shared export list compared" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: the production library boundary step runs tools/check_exports.py in build-and-test and build-and-test-windows; tools/check_exports.py, tools/exports.txt; 095f374 production sources separate from tests, strict endpoint port parsing")
    (:feature "Nightly soak" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: .github/workflows/nightly-soak.yml runs on the Linux, macOS and Windows fleet runners (846ae3d, 63a25be, 9ee42a2, 9e1b86f1, d6ffcfcc, 58ac8beb, 20f5c63d, c3409ab5)")
    (:feature "The library is callable from a shared library and a static library, from C and C++" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: tools/check_dll_consumer.py runs in build-and-test (Linux and macOS) and build-and-test-windows on every push; its macOS cases landed with eb50adb and its Windows cases with ae06e12" :note "one row for the macOS and Windows items")
    (:feature "Linux: with no BPF-capable clang, XDP is compiled out entirely and selecting it refuses cleanly; the build stays tolerant" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed with PR #432 (014c7d35); tests/test_unit_xdp_compiled_out.cpp (test_xdp_compiled_out_pin_refuses_not_built, test_xdp_compiled_out_list_takes_the_next_candidate, test_xdp_compiled_out_has_no_memory_plan) and tools/check_xdp_compiled_out.py in ci.yml, green in runs 40925425656 and 40928229963" :note "approved 2026-10-21 (plan #8, owner: not a build error, \"we want the build to be tolerant\"); no zero-length filter stub and no XDP code in the library")))
  (:id "api"
   :title "Public API"
   :text "The C surface in sdk/rocketnet.h and what a consumer needs to use it."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "Connection layer C surface: rocketnet_client_transport_* and rocketnet_server_transport_*" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; ruled #77; sdk/rocketnet.h; packet contexts checked against single-consumption leases: test_lifecycle.cpp check_packet_leases")
    (:feature "Root header pure C: the client and server with their functions, the address type, nothing else" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 5c3027f, dcd941f (6b73068); sdk/rocketnet.h plain C99 with one extern C block; test_public_client_server_queries; test_unit_config_env_names.cpp (5f84b75c); clean at /W4 and -Wextra 9ead512" :note "ruled: netcode-style, real non-mangled symbols for C and FFI; a C++ inside is an implementation privilege")
    (:feature "Message objects in C: rocketnet_message_client_* and rocketnet_message_server_*" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 2c1aa7b")
    (:feature "A fixed server key in the public server config: server_secret_key, all zeros generates a fresh pair, the development key refused in production" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #635 (c5f85ea4); test_public_server_secret_key_round_trips, test_public_server_secret_key_token_connects (ROCKETNET_DEV=ON) and test_public_server_dev_key_refused_in_production (ROCKETNET_DEV=OFF) in tests/test_unit_public_server_key.cpp, green on Linux, macOS and Windows in ci.yml runs 40928229963 and 40932598827")
    (:feature "The step-driven client and its receive stamp clock on the public client config, development builds only, refused at create in production" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #635 (c5f85ea4); test_public_step_driven_client_delivers_next_update (ROCKETNET_DEV=ON) and test_public_step_driven_refused_in_production (ROCKETNET_DEV=OFF) in tests/test_unit_public_server_key.cpp and tests/test_unit_public_step_driven_client.cpp, green on Linux, macOS and Windows in ci.yml runs 40928229963 and 40932598827; sdk/rocketnet_testing.h is deleted: rocketnet.h is the only header")
    (:feature "Installable CMake package with C and C++ consumers" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; tools/check_package.py, tools/package_consumer")
    (:feature "Vendored sodium, no system libsodium" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 23d4c40; sodium/")
    (:feature "Structured create errors and FFI-safe logging" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; status codes 4e2d6f1 (status_strings_cover_every_code); create_ex 3e82436, b2bc4ea, 33f84d3 (server_transport_create_ex_reports_every_status, client_transport_create_ex_reports_every_status, lifecycle_ex_reports_every_status); preformatted log callback 194ecc5 (log_callback_preformatted_contract)")
    (:feature "Transports are named transports throughout: the rocketnet_*_transport_* calls, ROCKETNET_SERVER_TRANSPORT and ROCKETNET_CLIENT_TRANSPORT, and the documentation" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux: landed as 92b6b50a; sdk/rocketnet.h names no driver; test_loopback_transport_env_pins in ./bin/test; Linux: the unit suite is green at 330e951e: ./bin/test exits 0 in a Release build on Linux x86_64, and the ASan and UBSan unit job of CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e passes; macOS: ./bin/test exits 0 at b12fb5a1 in a Release build on macOS arm64; Windows: the unit and functional suites green on Windows, landed 4529ca2d")
    (:feature "One receive queue per client and one per server, every channel's messages in delivery order, pumped in batches with no release call" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux: landed as 3a021484; receive_one_queue_every_type_every_channel, receive_pumped_past_one_batch_in_order, public_not_released_batch_released_by_update in ./bin/test; Linux: the unit suite is green at 330e951e: ./bin/test exits 0 in a Release build on Linux x86_64, and the ASan and UBSan unit job of CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e passes; macOS: ./bin/test exits 0 at b12fb5a1 in a Release build on macOS arm64; Windows: the unit and functional suites green on Windows, landed 4529ca2d")
    (:feature "Create returns NULL and a status code that names why it refused" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux: landed as 7c04293a; rocketnet_client_create and rocketnet_server_create take an enum rocketnet_status_t out-parameter; create_reports_status_success, create_reports_status_invalid_argument, create_reports_status_config_refusals, create_reports_status_out_of_memory and the other create_reports_status_ cases in ./bin/test; Linux: the unit suite is green at 330e951e: ./bin/test exits 0 in a Release build on Linux x86_64, and the ASan and UBSan unit job of CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e passes; macOS: ./bin/test exits 0 at b12fb5a1 in a Release build on macOS arm64; Windows: the unit and functional suites green on Windows, landed 4529ca2d")
    (:feature "A server serves IPv4, IPv6 or both on one port" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux: landed as 1581b134; second_public_address in rocketnet_server_config_t; server_serves_ipv4_and_ipv6_clients_on_one_port, one_family_server_is_unchanged, server_refuses_second_address_of_the_same_family in ./bin/test; Linux: the unit suite is green at 330e951e: ./bin/test exits 0 in a Release build on Linux x86_64, and the ASan and UBSan unit job of CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e passes; macOS: ./bin/test exits 0 at b12fb5a1 in a Release build on macOS arm64; Windows: the unit and functional suites green on Windows, landed 4529ca2d")
    (:feature "One environment variable per setting, current names only: retired names are not read" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux: landed as bd606975 and 5f84b75c, docs/BUILDING.md lists the current names (0158464f); config_env_every_name_read_is_documented, config_env_transport_passes_exercise_all_rows in ./bin/test; Linux: the unit suite is green at 330e951e: ./bin/test exits 0 in a Release build on Linux x86_64, and the ASan and UBSan unit job of CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e passes; macOS: ./bin/test exits 0 at b12fb5a1 in a Release build on macOS arm64; Windows: the unit and functional suites green on Windows, landed 4529ca2d")
    (:feature "Sized APIs for compatible struct evolution" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; a5941cf; sized_config_accepts_every_known_size, sized_config_refuses_unknown_size; docs/ABI-EVOLUTION.md")
    (:feature "Whole-transport memory estimates and operator budgets (#155)" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; rocketnet_server_required_memory and rocketnet_client_required_memory 1d9f830; the host memory estimate cad7a0c (rocketnet_test_server_host_memory_estimate_bounds_the_plan); operator budgets 227d895 docs/USAGE.md; docs/BUILDING.md Pre-allocation server resource plans" :note "an estimate of what is requested, with its exclusions named (kernel accounting beyond the requests, libbpf and libxdp, guard pages, application memory); not an available-RAM check")
    (:feature "C++ ClientTransport and ServerTransport interfaces" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 925cbd7 cpp_transport_interfaces_map_one_to_one, cpp_transport_fake_implements_the_interface; 8985b00 rocketnet_test_cpp_transports_connect_over_loopback")
    (:feature "Shared library build, checked exports, callable from C and C++" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 73733ad tools/check_header_exports.py; a26fd6c export count derived; a6e3991 tools/check_dll_consumer.py, tools/dll_consumer")
