  (:id "examples"
   :title "Examples"
   :text "The example series in examples/, each a small program that builds against the installed library; nightly-examples.yml runs them on Linux, and its macOS and Windows jobs are disabled."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "The example server runs out of the box" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: the happy-path job in ci.yml runs the example server and client on all three (1237a47); 14557ab")
    (:feature "hello: the least RocketNet program that works, and the home of the example series" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as 1581cc4, tested on Linux")
    (:feature "client + server: two programs over real UDP, with keys, a matchmaker stub and connect tokens" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as f2b109f, tested on Linux")
    (:feature "big_messages: a 200 KB reliable message, and an oversize unreliable send promoted" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as a3722bb, tested on Linux")
    (:feature "stats: state and counters through the public queries" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as e580649, tested on Linux")
    (:feature "budgets: send budgets and over-budget behaviour" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as a068af7, tested on Linux")
    (:feature "config_env: default, struct, environment, and a refused bad value" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as 64da826, tested on Linux")
    (:feature "transports: auto, a pin, and a list, chosen and said out loud" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as e87104d, tested on Linux")
    (:feature "channels: a stalled chat channel does not block positions" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as 96da6fb, tested on Linux")
    (:feature "ack receipts: did my unreliable update arrive?" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as bdef6ee, tested on Linux")
    (:feature "game_loop: a 60 Hz server and N clients, against the 100 microsecond client budget" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as ab83099, tested on Linux")))
  (:id "standard"
