    (:feature "The standard's vector index printed on demand, never committed" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: a tool that prints a document; landed as a11d924")
    (:feature "One standard: the old single-file standard retired into standard/" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: a document; landed as 3ce29a1")))
  (:id "keys-and-backends-planned"
   :title "Keys and backends"
   :text "What a game team needs to run its own connect-token backend: its own keypairs, the guide in docs/KEYS.md, and the example backends in Go and C# under examples/backend."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "Key generator: a rocketnet_keygen tool, built with the SDK, writing a fresh Ed25519 signing keypair and the token encryption key for production" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: keygen (tools/keygen.cpp) builds in the default CMake build on all three, and rocketnet_generate_backend_keypair, rocketnet_generate_server_keypair and rocketnet_write_production_connect_token are tested in tests/test_unit_public_connect_token.cpp (test_public_connect_token_round_trip, test_public_connect_token_wrong_server_key_refused, test_public_connect_token_wrong_protocol_id_refused, test_public_connect_token_null_or_short_buffer_refused, test_public_connect_token_sealed_block_varies) on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963; ./bin/keygen and the Go and C# --keygen modes pass in tools/run_backend_examples.py on Linux at c5f85ea4" :note "the server takes the public key; the private key stays on the backend; it replaces the published development keys. References: netcode's keygen and yojimbo's (tools/keygen.cpp is the starting point)")
    (:feature "Keys documentation: a KEYS.md guide to generating keypairs, where each key lives, rotation, and rocketnet_write_production_connect_token" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: a document; landed as 82b03dbb and updated with df4bae22 and c5f85ea4; docs/KEYS.md covers the backend Ed25519 keypair, the server X25519 keypair, keygen, rotation and rocketnet_write_production_connect_token, checked by tools/docs/check_agents_md.sh in docs.yml (green in run 40932599020 at c5f85ea4)" :note "a document. Covers where each key lives (backend, server, and never shipped in the client), rotation, and development keys versus production keys. References: netcode's and yojimbo's key documentation")
    (:feature "Example backends in Go and C#: a minimal HTTP backend in each that authenticates a player (stub), mints a connect token with the production keys for a chosen server address, and returns it for rocketnet_client_connect" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed with PR #430 (28e0d7d5) and 8f7b67e4; examples/backend/go and examples/backend/csharp; the backend-examples job in ci.yml runs go test -count=1 ./... and dotnet run --project Tests -c Release on every push (green in runs 40925425656, 40928229963 and 40932598827), and tools/run_backend_examples.py passes both development and --production modes on Linux at c5f85ea4" :note "each comes with a connect token format test vector shared with the C SDK, so tokens minted in Go and C# are accepted by the server. References: the netcode connect token and the yojimbo matcher backend (Go)")
    (:feature "Client example: fetches a connect token from the example backend and connects with it" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed with PR #430 (28e0d7d5) and 8f7b67e4; examples/backend_client.c and examples/backend_server.c; tools/run_backend_examples.py runs example_backend_server, each backend (Go and C#) and example_backend_client end to end over loopback in both development and --production (ROCKETNET_DEV=OFF) builds, passing backend_go_keygen, backend_go_token, backend_go_end_to_end, backend_csharp_keygen, backend_csharp_token and backend_csharp_end_to_end on Linux at c5f85ea4")))
  (:id "correctness-post-v1"
   :title "Correctness after v1.0.0-preview-1 (later)"
   :text "Correctness work that follows v1.0.0-preview-1."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "TLA+ invariants NoReceiveUnlessRunning and NoAdmitUnlessRunning on the server lifecycle, plus tests that a stopping or stopped server reads no packet and admits no client" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 462ac250; proofs/tla/ServerSession.tla (NoReceiveUnlessRunning, NoAdmitUnlessRunning), proofs/tla/MCServerSessionBrokenAdmitWhileStopping.cfg and proofs/tla/MCServerSessionBrokenReceiveWhileStopping.cfg in proofs/tla/RUNS.tsv, and tests/test_unit_client_server_lifecycle.cpp and tests/test_unit_driver_results_checked.cpp in ./bin/test on Linux, macOS and Windows (green in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963)" :note "the query itself ships as rocketnet_server_running in v1.0.0-preview-1")))
  (:id "preview-2-known-issues"
   :title "Preview-2 known issues (carried into preview-3 where still open)"
   :text "Current limits accepted for the preview-2 cut. These rows describe preview-2; the historical preview-1 table below is retained only as history."
   :label "known issue"
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "AF_XDP copy mode with one Windows portable client passed through 500 clients, but the 1000-client start failed after eight server connections hit reliable timeouts. The same Windows client passed 1000 clients against the portable Linux server." :cells (n - n))
    (:feature "The macOS Debug socket case reproduced a short receive while system-wide packet-drop counters surged under competing traffic. Quiet and focused repeats passed, so the correlation does not attribute the drops to RocketNet; a fix is not qualified." :cells (- n -))
    (:feature "The big-endian full-system run has no single all-green run yet: at 9232be69 the unit suite and the portable rung pass on s390x and the auto rung failed only test_server_port_zero_transport, whose compiled-out xdp refusal 8bbc8e41 now accepts (the case passes alone on the guest three of three); at af25b317 it passed alone three of three again. Known issue: one full-system guest run (unit, auto and portable rungs) of this head is still owed." :cells (n - -))
    (:feature "The full soak completed the portable, GSO, GSO-plain and io_uring 1000-client cells with non-timing PASS, then was killed during the AF_XDP cell. Cause: the fixed 16G virtme-ng guest is under the default profile's 16.96 GiB create-only plan, so the guest OOM-kills the load process (exit 137)." :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed with PR #601 (d2c1ca6b); .github/workflows/nightly-soak.yml sizes the xdp guest from LOAD_PLAN_ONLY=1 plus a measured run reserve (34G); at c3409ab5 on a 121 GB fleet runner the xdp cell passed three runs in a row in the 34G guest (peak RSS 26.1 GiB each, wall 1:56-2:09) and the full many-client step passed all five cells in 485 s")
    (:feature "Windows manual Debug/toolchain/examples/soak/frame-budget coverage, and some macOS and Windows LAN rows were not completed before the release cut." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The 100-microsecond server-update p99 target is missed at larger client counts. Correctness passes are reported separately from timing failures." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Windows native-server LAN qualification awaits the replacement test NIC; existing Windows client evidence does not qualify the server path." :cells (- - n))
    (:feature "Live AF_XDP qualification used copy mode only. Zero-copy and line-rate performance are unqualified. io_uring suite-concurrency and runner memlock provisioning work is deferred." :cells (n - -))))
  (:id "known-issues"
   :title "Historical preview-1 known issues and plans"
   :text "Historical preview-1 planning retained for context. Some fixes listed here landed before preview-2, so this table does not state current preview-2 status; use the preview-2 known-issues table above."
   :label "known issue"
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "Zero warnings at -Wconversion and the remaining strict flags, SDK and vendored libsodium (public header already clean at -Weverything)" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #454 (25c224c0); ROCKETNET_STRICT_WARNINGS is ON by default in CMakeLists.txt (-Wshadow -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wcast-qual -Wformat=2 -Wundef -Wdouble-promotion and /W4 as errors), green on all three at 126ef062 and 81b6d3ef (docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-3.md) and in ci.yml runs 40923772759 and 40925425656" :note "the default build is clean as errors on Linux (gcc, clang), macOS (Apple clang) and Windows (MSVC) at -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic, the strict flag set and /W4")
    (:feature "Client connect zeroes the client's 7.6 MB transport (about 3 ms) and disconnect wipes and frees it (about 1.6 ms). The final deliverable allocates the transport once at create, resets it in place on connect, and wipes only the secrets, by their size, on disconnect." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #527 (5abfcef4) and c9288575; sdk/rocketnet_client_transport.cpp, tests/test_unit_connection_reset.cpp, tests/test_unit_secrets_wiped.cpp and proofs/tla/RNDestroyWipe.tla, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Claiming and releasing a server slot re-initialises its 1.48 MB region inside the update (0.11 to 0.36 ms each), and disconnecting all of 1000 clients takes about 20 ms, plus about 130 ms in the next update. The final deliverable resets only the state a slot used." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #527 (5abfcef4) and c46df5d4; sdk/rocketnet_connection_reset.cpp, tests/test_unit_connection_reset.cpp, tests/test_unit_server_mass_disconnect.cpp, proofs/tla/RNLazyPool.tla and proofs/tla/RNWrittenRing.tla, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Large configurations still incur bulk memory wipes during shutdown. The 1000-client example soak can spike in memory and run out of memory on Linux. Secrets-only destroy is held for preview-3, not included in preview-2; completion polling does not remove the final synchronous cleanup cost." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #527 (5abfcef4) and c46df5d4; sdk/rocketnet_allocator.cpp wipes only secret and written extents on destroy, verified in tests/test_unit_secrets_wiped.cpp and proofs/tla/RNDestroyWipe.tla, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The default configuration needs about 13.4 GB for a 1000-slot server, because each client's send reserve is sized for 10 Gbps for 2 seconds. The public light-client profile sizes a 1000-slot server at 955,710,336 bytes (955,710 bytes per slot) for 1000 players at 10 Hz and a client at 3,063,168 bytes." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 22d812c8, af5fa4e2, 336aa3fa and 3b3f7e9d; rocketnet_client_light_config and rocketnet_server_light_config in sdk/rocketnet.h, verified in tests/test_unit_light_profile.cpp on Linux, macOS and Windows in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The server decrypts and seals packets on the game thread; the client already decrypts on its I/O thread. The final deliverable moves server decrypt and seal off the game thread." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "Native Linux server I/O uses bounded handoffs so the game thread does not wait on worker I/O or bulk copies. Messages and packets become visible after the worker completes the handoff, including on the following update. Exact-head p99 qualification remains pending." :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed as eaf420df, 8cf50f2f and b62f9b06; sdk/rocketnet_server_gso_linux.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_server_uring_linux.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_server_socket_linux.cpp and tests/test_unit_gso_handoff.cpp, qualified in docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-3.md and ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The portable server send and receive paths use bounded TX and RX workers instead of doing one game-thread system call per packet. Exact-head p99 qualification remains pending." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as eaf420df, 618529e3, 6f25a6f9 and 8cf50f2f; sdk/rocketnet_driver_builtin.cpp and tests/test_transport_control.cpp, qualified in docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-3.md and ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "One server update may process up to 16,000 received packets, each with its own decrypt, through three copies and extra keyed hashes per packet. The final deliverable bounds receive work per update by time as well as count, and removes the extra copies and hashes." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 88057df4 and ee3d0a3b; sdk/rocketnet_server_protocol.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_server_transport.cpp, tests/test_unit_server_receive_work.cpp and benchmarks/server_receive_cost.cpp, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The acknowledgement statistics sweep scans thousands of records per update. The final deliverable keeps those statistics up to date as acks arrive." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as d6dbd0a8 and 35465929; sdk/rocketnet_ack.cpp, tests/test_unit_server_stats_current.cpp, tests/test_unit_server_stats_no_worker.cpp and proofs/tla/RNServerStats.tla, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Every main call is meant to take under 0.1 ms in Release under load; the server API p99 does not yet meet that budget at 1000 clients. The final deliverable measures every main call at 1000 clients on each platform and holds the result in a gate." :cells (n n n) :note "The coordinator reports approximately 2 ms at 1000 clients, but no final exact-head receipt is available in this checkout; the cells remain unqualified")
    (:feature "Each unreliable message is sent as its own packet; small unreliable messages are not packed together. The final deliverable packs small messages into shared packets and keeps in-place writes for large ones." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #525 (556de284) and bb4bea8a; sdk/rocketnet_endpoint.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_message_server.cpp, tests/test_unit_unreliable_in_place.cpp, tests/functional/channel_unreliable_packing.cpp and proofs/tla/RNOutgoingBuild.tla, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Client disconnect and server stop request shutdown without waiting for workers; client disconnected and server stopped check completion without joining or freeing. Both client and server transports follow stop, stopped, destroy. Destroy asserts completion and synchronously joins and frees; a stalled worker leaves completion false and storage alive. The implementation has landed; exact-head platform qualification remains pending." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 5b48dd75, e8389a20, 8cf50f2f, 3d1c4e64 and PR #531 (dd5663b5); tests/test_unit_shutdown_request_completion.cpp, tests/test_unit_destroy_before_completion.cpp and proofs/tla/RNClientLinkStop.tla, qualified in docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-3.md and ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "On macOS, a portable-transport client connecting over IPv4 to a server that serves both IPv4 and IPv6 on one port failed to connect once, intermittently: observed once in a sharded functional run, not reproduced on rerun, and test_transport_dual_stack_ipv4_client passed in the full run at b0a8a2e3. The final deliverable finds the cause and proves every family combination on macOS by repeated functional runs." :cells (- y -) :evidence "macOS: landed as 60f9c345 and PR #630 (29cfeb83); docs/runs/macos-transport-cells-50x.md at 13b7b291 records 50 runs per cell across all family combinations (1000 runs) with 0 failures, and .github/workflows/nightly.yml runs macos-transport-cells-repeat")
    (:feature "On macOS, the historical full functional suite ran past CI's 120-second limit; it passed outside CI (all 142 cases at b0a8a2e3, about 6 m 38 s). The macOS CI restructuring is held for preview-3; preview-2 qualification depends on its own exact-head receipts." :cells (- y -) :evidence "macOS: landed as c662672e, 3a2300c3 and 980fb9c6; ci.yml runs the macOS functional suite across parallel jobs inside the per-commit budget (green in runs 40925425656 and 40928229963), and .github/workflows/nightly.yml runs macos-functional-nightly")
    (:feature "Some functional tests measure operating-system behaviour rather than RocketNet: test_macos_client_timing_default_qos, test_macos_client_timing_taskpolicy_background, the test_thread_priority_timing cases and test_thread_priority_windows_readback. The final deliverable removes them or rewrites them to test only RocketNet's own code." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as b12fb5a1 and 52d335c3 in 8cf50f2f; tests/functional/macos_client_timing.cpp and tests/functional/thread_priority_timing.cpp are retired, and tests/test_unit_platform_primitives.cpp tests RocketNet's own thread priority contract")
    (:feature "The macOS client timing functional test carries a branch that lowers the game thread's priority, which no case uses since its last caller was removed. The final deliverable removes the branch with the cases above." :cells (- y -) :evidence "macOS: landed as b12fb5a1 and 52d335c3 in 8cf50f2f; removed with tests/functional/macos_client_timing.cpp")
    (:feature "The Windows Debug, AddressSanitizer and Application Verifier runs passed before the last v1.0.0-preview-1 API changes and have not been repeated on the released API. The final deliverable repeats all three on the released API, on every Windows transport." :cells (- - y) :evidence "Windows: landed as 20e2a9a4, f90ec77e, 5c79349a, 6f4ab487 and 20f5c63d; .github/workflows/nightly.yml runs build-and-test-windows-debug and build-and-test-windows-asan, and tools/windows/appverif_run.py runs Application Verifier (docs/PLATFORMS.md)")
    (:feature "Client connect and server start still allocate: the client's transport, socket and I/O thread at each connect, and the server's transport and its tables at each start. The final deliverable builds them at create, so nothing allocates after create." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as c9288575; sdk/rocketnet_client_transport.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_server_transport.cpp, tests/test_unit_memory_plan_lifecycle.cpp and tools/check_memory.py, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "A few allocations do not go through the caller's allocator: AF_XDP packet memory, io_uring rings, the RIO registered region, thread stacks, interface discovery and the C library's output buffer. The final deliverable routes them through the caller's allocator where the operating system allows, and reports the rest by size." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as c9288575 and e3cb76dc; sdk/rocketnet.h, tests/test_unit_direct_allocations_counted.cpp and tests/test_unit_memory_plan_lifecycle.cpp, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The memory plan reports what create needs, but not yet what connect, reconnect, start and stop need. The final deliverable extends the plan to the whole session, so one block sized from the plan alone never runs out." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as c9288575 and 336aa3fa; rocketnet_client_required_memory and rocketnet_server_required_memory cover the whole session lifecycle, verified in tests/test_unit_memory_plan_lifecycle.cpp and tools/check_memory.py on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The handshake's signature-failure budget is kept per address and port, so one host rotating its ports can force up to 1024 signature checks per update. The final deliverable keys the budget by host address and caps signature checks per update." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 621c27b1 in 8cf50f2f and 7ca3e24d; sdk/rocketnet_server_protocol.cpp, tests/test_unit_signature_host_budget.cpp, tests/test_unit_handshake_budgets.cpp and proofs/tla/RNSecurityTables.tla, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Connect-token claims are first come, first served, so an observer on the network path can copy a client's first request and hold its token until the handshake deadline. The final deliverable's security pass closes this window or bounds it and documents it." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as f09f6f2d, ef0229e8 and 714a4f2c; sdk/rocketnet_server_protocol.cpp, standard/TRANSPORT.md, tests/test_unit_standard_handshake_server.cpp and proofs/tla/ReceiveOrder.tla, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "A replayed connection response refreshes a slot's receive time, a token claim is not released on three refusal paths, and a forged cookie can rewind a client's handshake (bounded). The final deliverable fixes each one, with a test for each." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as bd4c0823, c89bd81c and ea3145f5 in 8cf50f2f, ef0229e8 and 57ef874d; tests/test_unit_token_churn.cpp, tests/test_unit_standard_handshake_server.cpp, tests/test_unit_standard_handshake_client.cpp, proofs/tla/ServerConnection.tla and proofs/tla/ClientConnection.tla, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963" :note "the future-token part is tracked separately: PR #433 introduced the refusal and deleted the lifetime cap; preview-3 raises the server's explicit clock-skew allowance from five seconds to 30 seconds")
    (:feature "At very low send rates, time spent waiting for send budget counts toward the reliable-message timeout. The final deliverable counts only the time a message has been on the wire." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #537 (f8c4657a); sdk/rocketnet_endpoint.cpp and tests/test_unit_connection_reset.cpp, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Sequenced blocks and small records treat an in-turn record differently. The final deliverable gives both one rule, modelled and tested." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 370de240; sdk/rocketnet_channel_sequenced.cpp, tests/test_unit_channel_reliable_sequenced.cpp and proofs/tla/RNChannelTypes.tla, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Ack processing costs O(k²) per block, and the packet builder O(items²) per class pass. The final deliverable makes both linear." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as b9e01e67 in 8cf50f2f, PR #540 (8909c9bc), 2f4edba3, 26a63d80 and PR #614 (3b5433c9); sdk/rocketnet_ack.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_channel.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_packet_builder.cpp, tests/test_unit_packet_builder.cpp and tests/test_unit_ack_block_build_equivalence.cpp, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The example soak can fail when many clients disconnect at once: the server still counts connected clients after the disconnect pass. The final deliverable fixes the disconnect path and runs the example soak green on every platform." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 7e22c216 and cd02f6bd in 8cf50f2f and c46df5d4; examples/soak.c, sdk/rocketnet_server_transport.cpp and tests/test_unit_server_mass_disconnect.cpp, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The full client I/O TLA+ model needs a configuration that fits the CI time budget. The final deliverable splits it into configurations that each finish within the budget." :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed as 7e42de7e and 5e8fd6dd in 8cf50f2f and 9d10bc9a; proofs/tla/MCRNClientIo*.cfg, proofs/tla/README-RNClientIo.md and proofs/tla/RUNS.tsv, checked by tlc.yml (green in run 40937422459)")
    (:feature "The reconnect churn and UDP loopback functional cases showed rare timing failures under heavy machine load. The final deliverable makes them independent of machine load." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 7b407ca8 in 8cf50f2f, 64cd6624 and b159a67c; tests/functional/posix_lifecycle_stress.cpp, tests/functional/rocketnet_functional_tests.cpp and tests/time_scale.h, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The receipt read returns how many outcomes it copied, not how many there were when the caller's buffer is too short (ring overflow is counted, in receipts_dropped). The final deliverable returns the available count." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 13dd04bb in 8cf50f2f; sdk/rocketnet_window_ack.cpp, tests/test_unit_channel_receipts.cpp, tests/test_unit_client_server_lifecycle.cpp and docs/ABI-EVOLUTION.md, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Connect over whichever family works: send connection requests to the token's IPv4 and IPv6 addresses and keep the first that answers (TLA+ first)." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 3a04ed7a, 181ea6ea and 6f161fd1; sdk/rocketnet_client_transport.cpp, tests/test_unit_client_bind_family.cpp, proofs/tla/ClientConnection.tla and proofs/tla/ServerConnection.tla, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Backend keygen, connect-token minting and a reference server registration in Go and C#." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #430 (28e0d7d5), PR #521 (7be9f52e) and 8f7b67e4; examples/backend/go, examples/backend/csharp, tools/run_backend_examples.py and the backend-examples job in ci.yml, green in runs 40925425656, 40928229963 and 40932598827")
    (:feature "The v1.0.0-preview-1 API is provisional: names, structure and doc comments in the public header may still change. The final deliverable finalizes the API after customer feedback." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The receive path still accepts a datagram up to 1472 bytes (a 1439-byte payload), above the 1416-byte ROCKETNET_MAX_PACKET_PAYLOAD_BYTES every sender writes; the standard test vectors depend on the larger bound. The final deliverable refuses anything above the send bound and regenerates the vectors." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as c613a6a8 in 8cf50f2f; sdk/rocketnet_constants.h, standard/TRANSPORT.md, standard/pins/transport.tsv and tests/test_unit_max_payload.cpp, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The config field max_payload_bytes bounds the largest message, but max_message_bytes is already the name of a different field, so the rename to the message name waits. The final deliverable gives each of the two fields a name that says which limit it is." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 53f72306, df5e4461 in 8cf50f2f and 63cea137; sdk/rocketnet.h and tests/test_unit_public_message_limit.cpp, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Internal identifiers still use the old payload, ring, slot and window names that the public header no longer uses. The final deliverable renames them to the public terms in one pass." :cells (n n n))
    (:feature "The two config fields max_payload_bytes (the largest payload the transport fragments) and max_message_bytes (the largest message) are still separate; the final deliverable merges them into one max_message_bytes with one maximum, ROCKETNET_MAX_MESSAGE_BYTES, and states the max_payload_bytes limit through a define rather than the literal 305408." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 63cea137, PR #530 (d8385859) and PR #526 (8d9b0cc8); sdk/rocketnet.h, tests/test_unit_public_message_limit.cpp and tests/test_unit_message_boundary_sizes.cpp, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The client and the server measure packet_loss and jitter differently: the client measures loss of the server packets it receives and the change in arrival gaps, the server measures unacknowledged sends and round-trip spread. The final deliverable gives each stat one definition on both ends." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as c5176d03, dfdc9f2b and 8488861a in 8cf50f2f; sdk/rocketnet_ack.h, sdk/rocketnet_client_transport.cpp and tests/test_unit_ack_stats.cpp, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The development network simulator takes effect on a client connection at the next connect, and on a server at the next start, unless that connection already runs a simulator; the final deliverable applies it at once on a live connection too." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 3550a6f3; sdk/rocketnet_network_simulator.cpp, tests/test_unit_public_link_simulator.cpp and proofs/tla/MCLinkReconfigure.tla, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The internal headers have no extern \"C\" blocks, so a C tool cannot include them. The final deliverable adds them where a C caller needs one." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as e2f4aa97 in 8cf50f2f; sdk/rocketnet_connect_token.h and tools/internal_c/main.c, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Client connect from a handshake or token failure state (CONNECTION_DENIED .. CONNECT_TOKEN_EXPIRED) is refused until rocketnet_client_disconnect; the final deliverable lets connect start over from any failure state (TLA+ first)." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 9095b711 in 8cf50f2f and 76fd625b; sdk/rocketnet_client_protocol.cpp, tests/test_unit_client_server_lifecycle.cpp, tests/test_unit_connection_reset.cpp and proofs/tla/ClientConnection.tla, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The *_name lookups return two forms: status names are the enum suffix (\"OK\") and the client state, log level and disconnect reason names are lower-case words. The final deliverable returns the upper-case enum suffix from all four." :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as d1509a53 and 56da00ad; sdk/rocketnet.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_api.cpp and tests/test_unit_status.cpp, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "A Linux build with XDP off still needs the BPF and XDP development libraries. The final deliverable makes them optional when XDP is off." :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed as aec6e49b in 8cf50f2f and 35d77436; CMakeLists.txt, docs/BUILDING.md, tools/check_package.py and ci.yml, green in runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The public header carries a large volume of comments, some citing internal design references; the examples are longer than they need to be; the build has many targets. The final deliverable states each rule once in the header, shortens the examples and trims the build targets." :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed as 85c2f882 in 8cf50f2f, 3f406439, 6cd2744e and defd5aa8; sdk/rocketnet.h, tools/check_public_header.py, examples/*.c, tools/check_examples.py and CMakeLists.txt, green in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")))
  (:id "final-deliverable"
   :title "Final deliverable: hardening and long testing"
   :text "Soaks, load, stress, transport matrices, fuzzing, sanitizers, nightlies and the TLA+ ledger, run for the final deliverable after v1.0.0-preview-1. Every row here is planned for the final deliverable."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "A thousand clients for ten minutes on every transport of every platform, over the LAN, every guarantee checked" :cells (n n n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Linux: every transport cell fifty times in a row with zero flakes, and the functional suite under ASan per transport" :cells (n - -) :note "docs/runs/linux-transport-cells-50x.md at ac4206a69acd83840c27d2ea024f6cc3712d734f records fifty runs per socket cell (portable, gso and io_uring pairings and loopback) with zero failures and one ASan pass per cell, the xdp cell not made there; docs/runs/gso-asan-connect-cycle-stall.md at b159a67c records forty reruns of the one ASan stall case with zero stalls. Cited as delivery records, this final-deliverable row stays not-done until its own qualification")
    (:feature "macOS: every transport cell fifty times in a row, zero flakes, nightly" :cells (- y -) :evidence "macOS: landed as 60f9c345; docs/runs/macos-transport-cells-50x.md at 13b7b291 records fifty runs per cell (portable, msgx and loopback pairings, 1000 runs) with zero failures, .github/workflows/nightly.yml runs macos-transport-cells-repeat, and docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-3.md records verdict pass")
    (:feature "A thousand clients against a Windows server, on every Windows transport" :cells (- - n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Windows soaks per transport under loss, jitter and duplication, with flat handles and memory" :cells (- - y) :evidence "Windows: landed as d6ffcfcc and 58ac8beb; docs/runs/windows-soak-native-server.md at 3f900fa1 (1800 seconds per cell, iocp and rio) and docs/runs/windows-soak-portable.md at 74b8bb7f (1800 seconds, portable) record same-host loopback soaks under impairment with flat handles and memory, each PASS, .github/workflows/nightly-soak.yml runs soak-windows, and docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-3.md records verdict pass")
    (:feature "Every Windows transport, every address family, fifty times clean" :cells (- - y) :evidence "Windows: landed as 778c421f and de7025a4; docs/runs/windows-transport-family-50x.md at b225201d (portable and loopback cells) and docs/runs/windows-transport-family-50x-native.md at 689f0947 (iocp and rio cells) each record fifty runs per cell with zero failures, .github/workflows/nightly.yml runs windows-transport-cells-repeat, and docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-3.md records verdict pass")
    (:feature "Linux: thirty-minute soaks per transport under impairment with flat fds, threads and memory" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed as 720393a0, 98d797af and 7d70806b; docs/runs/linux-soak-30min-per-transport.md at adca4345 records 1800 seconds per cell (portable, gso, gso-plain, io_uring and xdp) under impairment with flat fds, threads and memory, every cell PASS, .github/workflows/nightly-soak.yml runs soak-per-transport, and docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-3.md records verdict pass")
    (:feature "Linux: 1000 light clients on every transport" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed as 22d812c8, af5fa4e2, 336aa3fa and d2c1ca6b; tests/test_unit_light_profile.cpp and tests/test_unit_memory_plan_lifecycle.cpp in ./bin/test on Linux (green in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963) and the 1000-client per-transport cells in .github/workflows/nightly-soak.yml (all five cells passing in 485 s at c3409ab5)")
    (:feature "Linux: a hard-killed client or an ICMP error never stalls portable, gso, io_uring or xdp" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed as af9df2d2 and ddb1da87; tests/functional/posix_hard_killed_client.cpp and docs/TRANSPORTS.md, green in ./bin/functional on Linux in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "macOS: 1000 clients per transport, three runs each, with the fd limit and counts in the summary" :cells (- n -) :note "docs/runs/lan-1000-proof.md records one macOS msgx run of 1000 clients for 600 seconds at 813b4adbe3dec2eee496577e3da2c0d7d66b8063; three runs per transport are not recorded, so this row stays not-done")
    (:feature "macOS: ASan, UBSan and TSan with Apple clang, and the leaks tool, on every suite and transport, nightly" :cells (- y -) :evidence "macOS: landed as cd424514 and 3b08c71f; .github/workflows/nightly-macos-sanitizers.yml runs ASan+UBSan, TSan and leaks across every suite and transport on macOS (docs/MACOS.md)")
    (:feature "Linux: the nightly soak jobs green at the branch" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: landed with PR #601 (d2c1ca6b); .github/workflows/nightly-soak.yml passes all five 1000-client cells (portable, gso, gso-plain, io_uring and xdp) in 485 s at c3409ab5, and docs/runs/linux-soak-30min-per-transport.md (adca4345) passes all five 30-minute impaired cells")
    (:feature "The fuzz targets build and run under libFuzzer on Windows" :cells (- - y) :evidence "Windows: landed as 3cc1b991; .github/workflows/fuzz-nightly.yml fuzz-windows builds and runs all fuzz targets under clang-cl and libFuzzer on Windows (tests/fuzz/README.md)")
    (:feature "Create, destroy, connect, restart: a thousand times on Windows with nothing left behind" :cells (- - y) :evidence "Windows: landed as dda29fba, 3cbf7a0a and 038131eb; tests/functional/windows_lifecycle_stress.cpp and tests/test_unit_process_resources_flat.cpp, green on Windows in ci.yml runs 40923772759 and 40925425656 and .github/workflows/nightly.yml")
    (:feature "Windows nightlies: all jobs run, warnings gated, verifier script safe" :cells (- - y) :evidence "Windows: landed as 6f4ab487, 20f5c63d and f90ec77e; .github/workflows/nightly.yml, .github/workflows/nightly-frame-budget.yml, .github/workflows/nightly-soak.yml and tools/windows/appverif_run.py")
    (:feature "TLA ledger: every case finishes or says why; docs current" :cells (y - -) :evidence ((Linux "Runtime source a76d641a has the same TLA tree as qualified b4c0a109: all 287 required cases across 44 groups passed with unchanged input hashes, no missing configurations and clean stale and ledger-merge checks. Eighteen of 21 separate bench cases retain explicit bounded-timeout results and are not counted as passes")))
    (:feature "Server send capacity is sized from the config, never a fixed 256" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 5606aa0c, af5fa4e2 and 8d9b0cc8; sdk/rocketnet.h, tests/test_unit_light_profile.cpp and docs/MACOS.md, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "macOS: 1000 light clients on msgx and portable" :cells (- y -) :evidence "macOS: landed as 22d812c8, 6f7f37e6, af5fa4e2 and 336aa3fa; tests/test_unit_light_profile.cpp and tests/test_unit_memory_plan_lifecycle.cpp verify the 1000-light-client msgx and portable plans and sessions on macOS in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963, and docs/runs/macos-soak-per-transport.md (31ad7862) records the msgx and portable soaks")
    (:feature "Windows: 1000 light clients on portable, iocp and rio" :cells (- - y) :evidence "Windows: landed as 22d812c8, af5fa4e2, 336aa3fa, 487f6990 and 3b3f7e9d; tests/test_unit_light_profile.cpp and tests/test_unit_memory_plan_lifecycle.cpp verify the 1000-light-client portable, iocp and rio plans and sessions on Windows in ci.yml runs 40923772759 and 40925425656, and docs/runs/windows-soak-native-server.md (3f900fa1) and docs/runs/windows-soak-portable.md (74b8bb7f) record the Windows per-transport soaks")
    (:feature "macOS: the nightly soak job green at the branch" :cells (- y -) :evidence "macOS: landed as 9e1b86f1 and 96404a61; .github/workflows/nightly-soak.yml soak-macos and docs/runs/macos-soak-per-transport.md at 31ad7862 (docs/MACOS.md, docs/QUALIFICATION-v1.0.0-preview-3.md)")
    (:feature "Ack receipts: LOSS only after the receipt deadline" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 47559484 and 8c5e3295; sdk/rocketnet_endpoint.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_window_ack.cpp, tests/test_unit_channel_receipts.cpp and proofs/tla/RNReceipts.tla, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The whole tree formatted with clang-format in the netcode style, the format checked in CI" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 126ef062 and 3cd21a3d; .clang-format, tools/format/check_format.sh and .github/workflows/ci.yml format check, green on all three in runs 40925425656, 40928229963 and 40932598827")))
  (:id "final-contraction"
   :title "Final contraction pass"
   :text "The last pass before v1.0.0: the library shrunk to the size and readability of netcode and yojimbo, one layer at a time from the bottom, with no change a caller can see. The public API, the wire format and every guarantee stay as they are; the existing unit, functional and soak suites and the TLA+ models guard each layer while it shrinks."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "Each layer's job written in one sentence, and the list corrected by the owner before any code changes" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: a document; landed with PR #602 (02297a13); docs/CLAUDE.md Layers 1 to 7")
    (:feature "Layer 1, init, allocator, logging and assertions: contracted" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #604 (acd02180; 3442b547, 0410ff3a, e1b91076); sdk/rocketnet_allocator.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_api.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_assert.h and sdk/rocketnet_log.cpp, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Layer 2, leaf utilities (address, hash, base64, bounded containers): contracted" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #605 (9bfa005c; 1e562a91); sdk/rocketnet_address.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_base64.cpp and sdk/rocketnet_hash.h, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Layer 3, platform (threads, mutexes, clocks, sockets): contracted, with far fewer preprocessor branches" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #606 (d9839106; 88ccf493) and PR #608 (5c4db328; 69702c2e, 220fc301); sdk/rocketnet_platform.cpp contracted to 2,658 lines with 32 conditional blocks, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Layer 4, transport protocol (token, cookie, handshake, keys, replay, acks, packets): contracted" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #607 (0c323522), PR #609 (b5d203c8), PR #611 (0084cc95) and PR #612 (38a49361); sdk/rocketnet_protocol.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_client_protocol.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_server_protocol.cpp and sdk/rocketnet_ack.cpp, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Layer 5, message layer (reliability, ordering, fragmentation, receipts, receive queue): contracted" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #613 (f0db4fb4), PR #614 (3b5433c9), PR #616 (961ad714) and PR #621 (b850e494); sdk/rocketnet_channel.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_endpoint.cpp, sdk/rocketnet_message_client.cpp and sdk/rocketnet_message_server.cpp, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "Layer 6, runtime transports: there is no driver; a driver is the transport. The sdk/rocketnet_driver* files and names are folded into the transports, each as small as its platform allows" :cells (n n n) :note "owner, 2026-10-28: \"I cut the concept of driver. A driver *is* the transport. There should be no driver.\" Six sdk/rocketnet_driver* files remain at f981340d")
    (:feature "Layer 7, public C API: contracted, with no change to rocketnet.h behaviour" :cells (n n n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Comments say what the code does, not why a review was satisfied" :cells (n n n) :note "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Tests and tools contracted alongside: library tests out of sdk/, unit cases run in layer order from layer 1 up, no case kept only for a deleted mechanism" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed with PR #513 (efecb7ad) and PR #603 (0c06f444); all test sources live under tests/ and tests/test_unit_registry.h runs unit cases in layer order from layer 1 up, green on all three in ci.yml runs 40925425656 and 40928229963")
    (:feature "The library is readable end to end in an afternoon: sdk/ total recorded before and after" :cells (n n n) :note "sdk/ is 98,906 lines at f981340d")))
